{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-crystal-basis-resolves-mass-tower-open-problems","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:crystal-basis-resolves-mass-tower-open-problems","kind":"proposition","title":"Crystal-basis correspondence (Brundan-Kleshchev + Type-B folding) reduces three mass-tower open problems to crystal-graph combinatorics","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/conj-kazhdan-lusztig-classical-limit"],"cites":["references/brundankleshchev2009","references/kashiwara1991","references/khovanovlauda2009","references/lecouvey2007","references/mayer1949"],"tags":["crystal-basis","klr-algebra","kashiwara-crystal","brundan-kleshchev","type-b-folding","kazhdan-lusztig","chirality-factor","term-7","z-habiro","open-problem-reduction"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.Archimedean.crystal_basis_reduction","text":"crystal-basis-resolves-mass-tower-open-problems.md","leanSource":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/crystal-basis-resolves-mass-tower-open-problems.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:crystal-basis-resolves-mass-tower-open-problems\"></a><p><em>The Brundan-Kleshchev isomorphism and Lecouvey bijection reduce three of the four open mass-tower problems to finite-graph combinatorics on Kashiwara crystals.</em></p>\n<p>The three reductions and the status of the fourth problem are described in\n<a href=\"#rem:crystal-basis-resolves-mass-tower-open-problems-context\">the crystal-reduction context</a>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/crystal-basis-resolves-mass-tower-open-problems.md","leanStatus":"proved","heading":"Proposition","number":"13.38.5"}
